+**Capabilities — canonical list as of round 50**
+
+Same four columns as the round-49 canonical list, which stays byte-intact; no row is added, and two rows are reworded for the tools the round-50 build landed: `append-only-audit` for v5 (line identity drops one trailing carriage return, a section title ignores `## ` lines inside CommonMark 0.31.2 §4.5 fenced code blocks, and a deleted line's origin is the union of the section titles holding it at every birth of it in the commit graph - a graph property, not a `rev-list` listing order) with its first-working round unchanged at 46, and `live-receipt-replay` for the process-bound witness (the live child runs `python -I` with an allow-listed environment and a parent-death signal, and the replay sets the same signal on itself, so killing whatever started it takes replay, live tool and server down) and the model mapping (the live tool records the file its server mapped from `/proc/<pid>/maps`, and a rerun must record it with `mapped` true and the receipt's model sha256) with its first-working round unchanged at 47. Eleven capabilities, as in round 49.
